{"type":"message","id":"fb57d7bc","parentId":"6652560a","timestamp":"2026-03-31T15:53:58.499Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the channels.feishu config now. It looks like it was partially updated but still has some old fields like `connectionMode`, `reactionNotifications`, `typingIndicator`, `resolveSenderNames`. Also the `dmPolicy` and `groupPolicy` are in the wrong place - they're under `default` account but should be at the top level or per account.\n\nLet me check what the current schema allows and fix it properly. The issue is:\n1. `connectionMode` - might still be invalid\n2. `reactionNotifications` - unknown if valid\n3. `typingIndicator` - might be valid per docs (mentioned as a quota optimization flag)\n4. `resolveSenderNames` - might be valid per docs (mentioned as a quota optimization flag)\n5. `dmPolicy` and `groupPolicy` in `default` account - these should probably be at top level\n\nAccording to the docs, the valid top-level fields for feishu are:\n- enabled\n- dmPolicy\n- domain\n- groupPolicy\n- groupAllowFrom\n- requireMention\n- accounts\n- defaultAccount\n- typingIndicator (optional flag)\n- resolveSenderNames (optional flag)\n\nAnd per-account fields:\n- appId\n- appSecret\n- name\n- domain (per account override)\n- typingIndicator (per account override)\n- resolveSenderNames (per account override)\n\nThe `default` account with `dmPolicy` and `groupPolicy` is wrong - these should be at the top level or per specific account, not in a `default` pseudo-account.\n\nLet me fix this properly:\n1. Move dmPolicy to top level\n2. Move groupPolicy to top level\n3. Remove the `default` account or restructure it properly\n4. Keep typingIndicator and resolveSenderNames at top level (they're valid per docs)\n5. Remove connectionMode and reactionNotifications if they're invalid\n\nActually wait - the error earlier said \"channels.feishu: invalid config: must NOT have additional properties\". So I need to remove any fields that aren't in the schema. \n\nLooking at the docs more carefully, `connectionMode` and `reactionNotifications` aren't mentioned anywhere, which suggests they're likely removed or invalid in this version. The `default` account structure with `dmPolicy` and `groupPolicy` is also problematic since those fields should be at the top level or on specific accounts, not bundled together. I need to restructure this to match what the schema actually expects.","thinkingSignature":"d34f280936b57ec5ece141e323961730258e68ce1284a769cb5b4765c3d77147"},{"type":"text","text":"channels 配置已经被部分修改，但还有问题。让我修正：\n\n**问题：**\n1. `default` 账户下的 `dmPolicy`、`groupPolicy` 位置不对\n2. `connectionMode`、`reactionNotifications` 可能已不支持\n3. 需要添加顶层 `dmPolicy` 和 `groupPolicy`\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_im499y0iad2m_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json","old_string":"\"channels\": {\n    \"feishu\": {\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"defaultAccount\": \"main\",\n      \"accounts\": {\n        \"main\": {\n          \"appId\": \"cli_a9243f0855b89e1b\",\n          \"appSecret\": \"YpMh4x85MwnG3DNjeERnDfNaJs2IM1OA\",\n          \"name\": \"Talus\"\n        },\n        \"lucus\": {\n          \"appId\": \"cli_a93108fad2b81e15\",\n          \"appSecret\": \"YXsvQgicI06FJkWenoDpggitFT6TCgVq\",\n          \"name\": \"Lucus\"\n        },\n        \"default\": {\n          \"dmPolicy\": \"pairing\",\n          \"groupPolicy\": \"open\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"domain\": \"lark\",\n      \"connectionMode\": \"websocket\",\n      \"reactionNotifications\": \"own\",\n      \"typingIndicator\": true,\n      \"resolveSenderNames\": true\n    }\n  }","new_string":"\"channels\": {\n    \"feishu\": {\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"domain\": \"lark\",\n      \"dmPolicy\": \"pairing\",\n      \"groupPolicy\": \"open\",\n      \"requireMention\": true,\n      \"defaultAccount\": \"main\",\n      \"typingIndicator\": true,\n      \"resolveSenderNames\": tr