{"type":"message","id":"7304b460","parentId":"64aa7b2e","timestamp":"2026-03-31T17:04:32.235Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the problem! The logs still show that it's trying to use `openai/gpt-5.4` as the primary model, not `minimax/MiniMax-M2.7`. The config change I made might not have been picked up properly.\n\nLooking at the logs:\n- `requestedProvider: \"openai\"`\n- `requestedModel: \"gpt-5.4\"`\n- `requestedModelMatched: true`\n\nThis means the config is still being read as using openai/gpt-5.4. The user said they restarted, but the old config is still being used.\n\nWait, looking more carefully, the log timestamps show these are old logs from around 17:04, and the config was edited... when? Let me check the timestamp of the config file.\n\nActually, the issue might be that the gateway wasn't fully restarted, or the openclaw-weixin channel has its own model binding that overrides the defaults.\n\nLooking at the bindings:\n```json\n\"bindings\": [\n  {\n    \"type\": \"route\",\n    \"agentId\": \"lucus\",\n    \"match\": {\n      \"channel\": \"feishu\",\n      \"accountId\": \"lucus\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"route\",\n    \"agentId\": \"main\",\n    \"match\": {\n      \"channel\": \"feishu\",\n      \"accountId\": \"main\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n```\n\nFor WeChat, the binding probably routes to the \"main\" agent. And the main agent might still be configured to use gpt-5.4 as its primary model.\n\nWait, I edited `agents.defaults.model.primary` but maybe the issue is that the bindings are routing to a specific agent that has its own model configuration, or the gateway isn't picking up the new config.\n\nActually, looking at the log event: `requestedProvider: \"openai\"`, `requestedModel: \"gpt-5.4\"`. This is from the fallback system trying models. \n\nThe logs are showing a cascade of failures - gpt-5.4 hits the rate limit, then openrouter/free also fails with \"Live session model switch requested\", and the same pattern repeats for stepfun and arcee-ai models. This suggests either a session lock-in to gpt-5.4 that's preventing fallback, or something wrong with how the fallback chain is configured. The timing is suspicious too - logs from 17:04 are being generated now at 17:17, which could mean there's a processing backlog or the system is retrying failed requests.\n\nThe config shows minimax/MiniMax-M2.7 as the primary with fallbacks to scnet and openrouter, but the actual requests are going to openai/gpt-5.4, which suggests either the config change wasn't picked up or there's another config source taking precedence. The RPC probe returning \"ok\" but gateway status showing \"unknown\" indicates the gateway might not have fully reloaded after the restart.","thinkingSignature":"33fca692be9239ee6cdfe75902aca9c53cbcfdbe2f6d59eab12dd7f7bf360554"},{"type":"text","text":"日志显示问题依然存在。奇怪，我明明修改了配置但还是在用 `gpt-5.4`。\n\n让我检查是否有其他地方在覆盖模型设置：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6ic3nkq88ni4_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"gpt-5.4\" /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":65048,"output":690,"cacheRead":11957,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77695,"cost":{"input":0.019514399999999998,"output":0.000828,"cacheRead":0.00071742,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.021059819999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774976655692,"responseId":"061b3190b90cbe43a4da0a13458b2de3"}}
