{"type":"message","id":"a425adf4","parentId":"9a1f258c","timestamp":"2026-03-31T17:04:51.617Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The config looks correct - primary is minimax/MiniMax-M2.7. But the logs are still showing openai/gpt-5.4 being used. \n\nWait - maybe the issue is that there's an auth profile for openai that has a rate limit cooldown in effect. The logs show `profileFailureReason: \"rate_limit\"` and `failureCounts: {rate_limit: 6}`.\n\nSo even though the config says to use minimax, it's trying to use openai first (maybe because of a session or context that was using openai before). And that openai auth profile is in cooldown.\n\nActually looking more carefully at the log - it's the WeChat channel that's causing issues. And the error shows the model being used is gpt-5.4, not minimax.\n\nWait - I think I understand now. The logs show that the system is trying to use gpt-5.4, then going through fallbacks. But if the cooldown for openai is in effect, it might be blocking all requests.\n\nActually the real problem might be that the config WAS changed but the GATEWAY didn't pick it up because the user needs to do a proper restart, not just `docker compose restart`.\n\nOr maybe the issue is that the minimax API key isn't working properly. Let me check if there's any error with minimax.\n\nActually, let me look at the auth profiles in the config.","thinkingSignature":"74e27a724e1f158cbb4e06d61f61d4f1c1c8c6e5d3b32fef9fe0f4ae2e559639"},{"type":"text","text":"配置是正确的。问题可能是 **OpenAI API 配额已耗尽**，系统虽然尝试 fallback 但可能 cooldown 还在生效。\n\n让我检查 auth profile 状态：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_unz3veqh9kd2_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -A10 '\"auth\"' /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json | head -15"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":66188,"output":366,"cacheRead":11957,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":78511,"cost":{"input":0.0198564,"output":0.0004392,"cacheRe