{"type":"message","id":"8e714fb5","parentId":"a425adf4","timestamp":"2026-03-31T17:04:51.665Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_unz3veqh9kd2_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"auth\": {\n    \"profiles\": {\n      \"minimax:cn\": {\n        \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n        \"mode\": \"api_key\"\n      },\n      \"openai:default\": {\n        \"provider\": \"openai\",\n        \"mode\": \"api_key\"\n      },\n      \"openrouter:default\": {\n--\n    \"auth\": {\n      \"mode\": \"token\",\n      \"token\": \"12ecb07625acf2468a5a6472abdad19f9cf6e409cd17b60996a3144a85e9209b\""}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":38,"aggregated":"\"auth\": {\n    \"profiles\": {\n      \"minimax:cn\": {\n        \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n        \"mode\": \"api_key\"\n      },\n      \"openai:default\": {\n        \"provider\": \"openai\",\n        \"mode\": \"api_key\"\n      },\n      \"openrouter:default\": {\n--\n    \"auth\": {\n      \"mode\": \"token\",\n      \"token\": \"12ecb07625acf2468a5a6472abdad19f9cf6e409cd17b60996a3144a85e9209b\"","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774976691661}}
{"type":"message","id":"d6e80aee","parentId":"8e714fb5","timestamp":"2026-03-31T17:05:04.818Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see auth profiles for minimax and openai. The issue is that the openai profile has been rate limited and is in cooldown. But the config says to use minimax first.\n\nWait - let me re-read the log more carefully:\n\n```\n\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\"\n\"provider\":\"openai\"\n```\n\nBut my config says primary should be `minimax/MiniMax-M2.7`. Why is it trying to use openai/gpt-5.4?\n\nActually, looking at the fallback chain - it shows the system tried:\n1. openai/gpt-5.4 - failed with rate_limit\n2. openrouter/free - failed with \"Live session model switch requested\"\n3. stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free - failed same way\n4. arcee-ai/trinity-mini:free - failed same way\n\nThis suggests the primary model (minimax) is NOT being tried at all. Why?\n\nWait - looking at `requestedProvider: \"openai\"` and `requestedModel: \"gpt-5.4\"` - this is coming from somewhere as the REQUESTED model, not the result of fallback.\n\nOh! I think I understand now. The log shows \"model_fallback_decision\" - this means the system is trying to decide what to do when the requested model fails. But what is the \"requested\" model? It might be coming from a session binding or something.\n\nActually, wait - the lane is `session:agent:main:openclaw-weixin:...` so it's using the main agent for the weixin channel. But the main agent's model should be minimax...\n\nUnless there's a session state that's locked to gpt-5.4 from before. Or the config restart didn't fully reload.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The user said they restarted. Maybe they need to also clear some state?\n\nActually, let me check if there's a way to see the current runtime model being used. Or maybe I should suggest the user to explicitly set the model for the weixin channel.\n\n\nThe minimax configuration might not be properly set up in the providers section, which could be forcing the system to fall back to openai even though minimax is specified as primary.","thinkingSignature":"8afcc7dbb904c6aaee26f30ca9904c1853d8a8c71a21a733f0772d80ba47d76d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_h2ma0d6deoez_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -A5 '\"minimax\"' /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json | head -15"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":66693,"output":505,"cacheRead":11957,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":79155,"cost":{"input":0.0200079,"output":0.000606,"cacheRead":0.00071742,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.021331319999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774976691666,"responseId":"061b31b4a2177b22541cd392fadc206f"}}
