{"type":"compaction","id":"db20068f","parentId":"0945ae0e","timestamp":"2026-04-01T00:05:26.710Z","summary":"## Goal\n1. Fix OpenClaw 3.28 configuration issues (channels.feishu schema changes)\n2. Configure WeChat (weixin) channel integration\n3. Resolve duplicate plugin warning\n4. Change main agent's default model to MiniMax-M2.7\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Docker container installation\n- Use `docker compose` not `docker-compose` (new Docker CLI syntax)\n- Privacy protection: do not expose sensitive credentials (appId, appSecret, API keys) in responses\n- User prefers to update by pulling new Docker image rather than `openclaw update`\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Checked cron tasks: daily-backup (error) and config-backup-8am (ok)\n- [x] Identified 3.28 breaking changes: qwen-portal-auth removed, config migration stricter\n- [x] Fixed channels.feishu config for 3.28 compatibility:\n  - Removed: connectionMode, streaming, footer, threadSession, reactionNotifications\n  - Changed: botName → name in accounts\n  - Moved: dmPolicy, groupPolicy from \"default\" account to top level\n  - Removed invalid \"default\" account\n  - Kept: typingIndicator, resolveSenderNames\n- [x] Deleted qwen-portal-auth from plugins.entries\n- [x] Installed @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin plugin (v2.1.1)\n- [x] Deleted staging directory `/home/node/.openclaw/extensions/.openclaw-install-stage-pFltcW/`\n- [x] Verified weixin plugin enabled in config\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] User needs to restart container (`docker compose restart`) to apply plugin changes\n- [ ] User needs to run `openclaw channels login --channel openclaw-weixin` on host to scan QR code\n- [ ] Changing main default model from openai/gpt-5.4 to minimax/MiniMax-M2.7 (was searching config when session ended)\n\n### Blocked\n- Cannot restart Docker container from inside container (needs host command)\n- Cannot display QR code for WeChat login from inside container\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Use Docker image update instead of openclaw update**: User prefers `docker compose up -d` after pulling new image\n- **Manually edit config instead of doctor --fix**: Container couldn't start after upgrade, so direct file edits were made\n- **Preserve appSecret/appId values**: Did not repeat sensitive values in responses\n\n## Next Steps\n1. User must run `docker compose restart` on host to apply plugin directory deletion\n2. After restart, user should run `openclaw channels login --channel openclaw-weixin` on host to complete WeChat QR code login\n3. Change line 220 in `/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json`: `\"primary\": \"openai/gpt-5.4\"` → `\"primary\": \"minimax/MiniMax-M2.7\"`\n4. Verify all config warnings are resolved after restart\n\n## Critical Context\n- Config file: `/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json`\n- Plugins directory: `/home/node/.openclaw/extensions/`\n- Weixin plugin path: `/home/node/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`\n- Model config line 220: `\"primary\": \"openai/gpt-5.4\"` (needs change to minimax/MiniMax-M2.7)\n- Duplicate plugin warning still pending container restart to verify fix\n- WeChat QR code URL for scanning: `https://liteapp.weixin.qq.com/q/7GiQu1?qrcode=...`\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nThe user asked to check why WeChat (微信) is bound but not responding to messages.\n\n## Early Progress\n- Assistant ran `openclaw gateway status` — Gateway is running (RPC probe: ok, listening on port 18789)\n- Assistant checked WeChat logs: Found repeated errors showing **\"You exceeded your current quota, please check your plan and billing details\"** — this is an OpenAI API quota exceeded error affecting the WeChat lane (session:agent:main:openclaw-weixin)\n\n## Context for Suffix\nThe WeChat plugin is bound and the gateway is operational, but incoming messages are failing because the AI agent (running on the openclaw-weixin lane) cannot process them — the OpenAI API quota has been exceeded, causing a `FailoverError`. The suffix likely continues with more log analysis or a resolution attempt.\n\n<read-files>\n/home/node/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json\n</read-files>\n\n<modified-files>\n/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n</modified-files>","firstKeptEntryId":"e74e9400","tokensBefore":87636,"details":{"readFiles":["/home/node/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json"],"modifiedFiles":["/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json"]},"fromHook":false}
